# arch-bootstrap configuration
#
# Copy to `bootstrap.conf` and fill in. That file is gitignored -- it holds the
# person- and machine-specific values, which is what keeps bootstrap.sh itself
# free of anything private and safe to publish.
#
# You do not have to create it by hand: run ./bootstrap.sh and stage 00 will
# offer to generate it interactively on first run.
#
# Every value here can also be supplied as an environment variable, which takes
# precedence over nothing -- the config file is sourced after the defaults, so
# the file wins. Export a value and comment the line out here if you want the
# environment to win.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required-ish

# Bare git repo holding your dotfiles, checked out with --work-tree=$HOME.
# SSH remotes are the normal case, and are why stage 05 is a hard gate.
DOTFILES_REMOTE="git@github.com:you/your-dotfiles.git"

# Repo holding your password vault and other secrets. Leave empty to skip
# stage 35 entirely.
SECRETS_REMOTE=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# Git remote holding desktop wallpapers. .xinitrc points nitrogen at
# WALLPAPERS_DIR (default $HOME/projects/wallpapers); without this the desktop
# comes up with no wallpaper and nothing says why. Leave empty to skip.
WALLPAPERS_REMOTE=""

# Absolute path to an Obsidian vault. Leave empty to skip the Obsidian sync
# stages (55 and the unit generation in 60) completely.
OBSIDIAN_VAULT=""

# Set ONLY if you use a non-standard config root, e.g. "$HOME/.configure".
# Leave empty for the standard ~/.config.
#
# If you do set it, note that systemd user units still live in ~/.config/systemd/user
# regardless -- systemd does not honour XDG_CONFIG_HOME for unit lookup. The script
# already handles that; it is called out here because it surprises people.
CONFIG_HOME_OVERRIDE=""

# Shell to chsh into during stage 40.
LOGIN_SHELL="zsh"

# URL of a precompiled SSH key-transfer helper binary, if you have one. Stage 05
# fetches it over plain HTTPS before anything else, because it needs no
# credentials to download -- that is what breaks the chicken-and-egg where
# cloning your dotfiles requires a key that lives in your dotfiles.
#
# Leave empty and stage 05 will instead offer to ssh-keygen and walk you through
# registering the public key by hand.
KEYXFER_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- paths

#DOTFILES_DIR="$HOME/.dot"
#SECRETS_DIR="$HOME/secrets"
#WALLPAPERS_DIR="$HOME/projects/wallpapers"
#XMONAD_DIR="$HOME/.xmonad"

# Major node version to pin. Native modules (better-sqlite3 in obsidian-headless,
# for one) are compiled against a specific NODE_MODULE_VERSION, so a floating
# node breaks them with ERR_DLOPEN_FAILED.
#NODE_MAJOR="24"
